  "notes": [
    "Flavor Profile: High-altitude Peruvian Arabica medium roasts are known for a smooth, well-rounded body with gentle acidity and classic tasting notes of cocoa, toasted nuts, and subtle caramel sweetness.",
    "Brewing Ratio: A standard coffee-to-water ratio of 1:15 to 1:17 by weight (approximately 1 to 2 tablespoons of ground coffee per 6 ounces of water) produces a balanced, everyday cup.",
    "Water Temperature: Brew with filtered water heated to 195°F–205°F (90°C–96°C) to extract sweetness and aroma without scalding the grounds.",
    "Grind Selection: Grind immediately before brewing to match your method—coarse for French press or cold brew, medium for automatic drip, medium-fine for pour-over, and fine for espresso.",
    "Medium Roast Profile: Unlike light roasts (which highlight sharp, bright fruit acidity) or dark roasts (which emphasize smoky bitterness and roast oils), a medium roast balances natural origin sweetness with a rich, caramelized body.",
    "Storage: Whole beans preserve their natural aromatic oils and peak flavor far longer than pre-ground coffee; keep beans sealed in an airtight container in a cool, dark cupboard away from moisture and heat."
